{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.WedderburnAsNoncommFourier","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.WedderburnAsNoncommFourier","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic"],"declarations":15,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.peter_weyl_decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.peter_weyl_decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L78-L88","doc":"A re-export theorem in the same shape used by\n`QOU.WedderburnMass.atomicMass`: given the inverse-Fourier\ninterface, the trace of `β` is reconstructed from its\nnon-commutative Fourier coefficients `{χ_λ(β)}`.\n","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier","label":"prop:wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Decomposition: trace as a weighted sum of `χ_λ / d_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.nodup_indexFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.nodup_indexFin","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The indexing list contains no duplicates: the Peter–Weyl sum\nranges over the *set* of distinct irreducibles, so duplicate\nentries would overcount. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.indexFin","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.indexFin","kind":"def","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L68-L68","doc":"Existence of a finite indexing set on which the sum is taken. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier.mk","kind":"ctor","line":66,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L66-L66","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.IsInverseFourier","kind":"class","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L52-L76","doc":"The **inverse non-commutative Fourier transform reading**: the\ntrace evaluates as a weighted sum of character values. The sum is\n*finite* because `spectrum` is a partition lattice for fixed `n`\n(instantiated `Fintype` at use sites). We expose the equation as a\nfield so downstream theorems can pattern-match on it without\ndepending on a concrete `Fintype` instance.\n\n**Status.** This is the Peter–Weyl/Plancherel formula for a\nfinite-dimensional semisimple algebra. Proving it generically\nrequires Mathlib infrastructure for character orthogonality on\nHecke algebras that is not yet in place. We therefore state the\ndecomposition as a typeclass-style field; concrete instances\n(e.g. for `H_n(q)` at small `n`) supply the proof.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.dim_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.dim_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":50,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L50-L50","doc":"All quantum dimensions are non-zero (semisimplicity). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.weight","kind":"def","line":48,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L48-L48","doc":"Plancherel/Markov weight `w_λ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.dim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.dim","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L46-L46","doc":"Quantum dimension `d_λ` of the `λ`-block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.chi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.chi","kind":"def","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L44-L44","doc":"Character on the `λ`-block. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.spectrum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.spectrum","kind":"def","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L42-L42","doc":"Index type for the non-commutative spectrum (e.g. `λ ⊢ n`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.tr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.tr","kind":"def","line":40,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L40-L40","doc":"Trace functional (e.g. the Jones–Markov trace). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.carrier","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.carrier","kind":"def","line":38,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L38-L38","doc":"Carrier of the algebra (e.g. `H_n(q)`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L36-L36","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.WedderburnFourier.NonCommFourierData","kind":"structure","line":27,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/wedderburn-as-noncomm-fourier.lean#L27-L50","doc":"Abstract data of a Wedderburn–Artin / Peter–Weyl decomposition of\na finite-dimensional semisimple algebra `A` together with a trace\n`τ : A → ℝ`. We package the data so that any callers only depend\non the *interface* (partitions = spectrum, characters = Fourier\ncoefficients, weights = Plancherel measure), not on the underlying\nHecke-algebra construction.\n\nConcrete instances for `H_n(q)` at generic `q` are constructed in\n`QOU.WedderburnMass`; this file is the abstract glue. ","signatureChunk":0}]}